= Modern Computing

The digital revolution began in earnest during the mid-20th century.
Integrated circuits enabled exponential growth in transistor density.
Personal computers transformed everyday life and the nature of work.

The internet connected billions of devices across the entire globe.
Open-source software democratised access to powerful development tools.
Artificial intelligence is now reshaping every major industry sector.

Quantum computing promises to break current cryptographic assumptions.
Fault-tolerant quantum processors may arrive within the next two decades.
